Wait, the usage error message in `if (!repo || ...)` should include "head-tree"? The separate check handles it (with its own log). But the first usage message names the required args — update it to mention head-tree. Let me update that message.

Also the arg-missing check for head-tree currently reports "cannot check for conflict markers" without usage. Fine, but let's make the initial usage line complete:

"usage: validate_pull_request.ts --repo owner/name --number N --branch B --workflow W --def-dir DIR --deliverable-report FILE --head-tree DIR"

Now the comment-posting decision. Find the block:

```ts
  if (outcome.verdict !== "passed") {
    reportFailure(repo, values.number ?? "", runUrl, outcome.summary, deliverableProblems);
  }
```

Replace with:

```ts
  if (conflictMarkers.length > 0) {
    reportConflictMarkers(
      repo,
      values.number ?? "",
      conflictMarkers,
      outcome.verdict !== "passed" ? runUrl : "",
    );
  } else if (outcome.verdict !== "passed") {
    reportFailure(repo, values.number ?? "", runUrl, outcome.summary, deliverableProblems);
  }
```

With a comment explaining why the brief is replaced.

Note: `reportFailure` also carries `deliverableProblems` details. When markers exist, we suppress them. Add a sentence to the comment.

